                <pb facs="0597" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg485"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-07-14"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 14,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s July 13. Brazilian chargé d’affaires not available. I therefore this
                    morning alone conferred with minister for foreign affairs of Ecuador. Minister
                    for foreign affairs of Ecuador agreed to refrain from any further attacks,
                    provided that the arrangements would soon be perfected without restriction. Said
                    that people of Ecuador greatly excited, and that if situation continued the
                    Government would be unable to calm popular mind and did not know when uprising
                    might occur; that a few days since police had dispersed a meeting whose object
                    was to demand war. Repeated Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
